.TH TIMESHIFT-ON-DEMAND-PROMPT 1 "August 2026" "timeshift-on-demand" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
timeshift-on-demand-prompt \- zenity-confirmed on-demand Timeshift backup, headless
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B timeshift-on-demand-prompt
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads the backup drive configured via the
.BR timeshift-on-demand (1)
Settings tab, waits for it to mount, asks for confirmation with
.BR zenity (1),
and on confirmation spawns a live monitor terminal window before
running the backup via
.BR pkexec (1).
.PP
Not meant to be run interactively by hand \(em it is invoked
automatically at login (via an XDG autostart entry) and after resume
from suspend (via a systemd-logind sleep hook), independent of whether
the main
.BR timeshift-on-demand (1)
window is open.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/timeshift-on-demand/config.json
Read for the configured backup drive UUID.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/timeshift-on-demand/backup.log
Backup run history, shared with the GUI app.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR timeshift-on-demand (1),
.BR zenity (1),
.BR pkexec (1)
